UID:quin-event-205635@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261002T170000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Taste of Crete
LOCATION:Café Q
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nTime: 5 PM – 9 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/205635\n\nThis October\, Café Q invites members to experience A Tast
 e of Crete\, a limited-time menu inspired by the sun-soaked flavors and vi
 brant culinary traditions of Greece’s largest island.\n\nAvailable exclu
 sively during dinner service\, this thoughtfully curated menu celebrates t
 he fresh\, uncomplicated spirit of Cretan cuisine—think fresh-caught sea
 food\, seasonal vegetables\, fragrant herbs\, local cheeses\, and exceptio
 nal olive oils\, all rooted in the island’s connection to land and sea. 
 Pair your meal with a crisp Greek white and settle in for a taste of the M
 editerranean\, no passport required.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/205635
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206908@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261015T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261015T200000
SUMMARY:Fashion Salon: An Evening with MONSE
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 3 spots left\nSt
 atus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/20
 6908\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Programming\, 7:30PM Boutique Shopping\n
 Join us for an immersive fashion salon with MONSE\, the New York–based f
 ashion house known for its deconstructed tailoring\, unexpected proportion
 s\, and singular take on modern femininity. Co-Founder and Co-Creative Dir
 ector Fernando Garcia will present the Fall/Winter 2026 collection\, salon
  style and share the inspirations\, craftsmanship\, and stories behind som
 e of the season’s most distinctive pieces\, offering members a rare glim
 pse into his creative process. In a nod to the intimate maison presentatio
 ns that helped shape the modern runway\, models will move throughout The R
 eading Room\, inviting members to settle in\, relax\, and experience the c
 ollection up close.\n\nAt the heart of the collection is the sunflower\, h
 and-painted by Garcia and reimagined as a symbol of resilience\, longevity
 \, and enduring vitality. The motif appears throughout in rich shades of m
 arigold\, burgundy\, red\, brown\, and grey\, across fluid silks\, intrica
 te embroidery\, dimensional knits\, deconstructed tailoring\, and sculptur
 al eveningwear.\n\nFollowing the presentation\, members are invited to con
 tinue the evening in The Terrace with an exclusive MONSE shopping experien
 ce and the opportunity to explore the collection firsthand with the MONSE 
 team.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Compl
 imentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that a
 ll cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206908
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-195628@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261017T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T120000
SUMMARY:Hands On Impact: Cradles to Crayons
LOCATION:Offsite - The Giving Factory
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 10 sp
 ots left\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/195628\n\nMake an impact with Cradles to Crayons through a hands
 -on volunteer opportunity. Cradles to Crayons is a nonprofit committed to 
 ending children’s clothing insecurity in the U.S. Since 2002\, they have
  provided more than 6 million packages of essentials - including clothing\
 , shoes\, diapers\, and school supplies - to children across the country.\
 n\nAt the Cradles to Crayons “Giving Factory\,” you will take part in 
 sorting\, quality-checking\, and packaging donations that go directly to c
 hildren and families in need - helping ensure every child can arrive at sc
 hool feeling confident\, prepared\, and valued.\n\n*This event is complime
 ntary and reserved for members\, plus one registered guest age 6+. Please 
 wear comfortable clothing you don’t mind getting dirty\, along with clos
 e-toed shoes. The warehouse is not climate controlled\, so dress with the 
 weather in mind.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/195628
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
