BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206823@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T210000
SUMMARY:Live Music: Carlos Odria 
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Available\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206823\n\nPeruvian-born
  guitarist Carlos Odria brings his distinctive sound to The ’House for a
 n evening of live music blending jazz with rhythms from across Latin Ameri
 ca and beyond. Moving effortlessly between bossa nova\, Afro-Peruvian fest
 ejo\, rumba flamenco\, and Afro-Caribbean influences\, Odria pairs remarka
 ble technique with an improvisational style rooted in the rich tradition o
 f American jazz.\n\n*Please note that this event is complimentary and rese
 rved for members\, plus three guests. Seating is first come\, first served
 .
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206823
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206916@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261028T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Wealth\, Well Lived
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 45 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/2
 06916\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nWhat does it really mean to
  live a wealthy life? In the first of a new\, multi-part series presented 
 with Willow and The Impact Collective we will look beyond what we earn\, 
 save\, or invest\, to consider how wealth reflects the choices we make\, t
 he opportunities we create\, and the values we carry into our personal and
  professional lives. Joined by Lacy Garcia\, Founder and CEO of Willow\, a
 nd Julia Johannsen\, Founder and Executive Director of The Impact Collecti
 ve\, this discussion will explore the intersection of money\, investing\, 
 and personal values. Together\, they will begin to decode the systems that
  shape our financial lives and consider how greater understanding can lead
  to more informed\, purposeful decisions. As the series unfolds\, expect t
 o explore conversations such as the wealth gap\, generational planning\, r
 oles and representation\, and the ways we can rethink traditional ideas of
  wealth to better align our investments with the lives and\, legacies we w
 ant to build.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members onl
 y. Complimentary light bites will be served\, with beverages available for
  purchase throughout the evening. We kindly ask that all cancellations be 
 made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206916
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
